            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Ok, let's try debugging further.\r\n\r\nFirst, just to be sure, could you please check that you indeed using the latest `main` branch? The best way to do this is to look at the code of 'mini.starter' module (should be in 'lua/mini/starter.lua' subdirectory of where 'mini.nvim' plugin is installed) and see that [these lines](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/6cb7cdb1cd7f111784d5d971fa41a655e11df4b3/lua/mini/starter.lua#L1209-L1213) are present.\r\n\r\nIf it is indeed latest, could you please set explicitly `vim.o.showtabline = 2` before calling `require('mini.starter').setup()` and see if it fixes this issue.",
